# STOCKHOLM 1.0
#=GF ID FMN
#=GF AC RF00050
#=GF DE FMN riboswitch aptamer (RFN element)
#=GF AU Ontiveros-Palacios N; 0000-0001-8457-4455
#=GF GA 66.2
#=GF NC 66.1
#=GF TC 66.2
#=GF PI RFN
#=GF SE Vitreshchak A
#=GF SS Published; PMID:12456892
#=GF TP Cis-reg; riboswitch;
#=GF BM cmbuild -F CM SEED
#=GF CB cmcalibrate --mpi CM
#=GF SM cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -T 30.00 -Z 2958934 CM SEQDB
#=GF DR SO; 0000035; riboswitch;
#=GF DR GO; 0010181; FMN binding;
#=GF RN [1]
#=GF RM 12136096
#=GF RT Regulation of riboflavin biosynthesis and transport genes in bacteria by
#=GF RT transcriptional and translational attenuation.
#=GF RA Vitreschak AG, Rodionov DA, Mironov AA, Gelfand MS
#=GF RL Nucleic Acids Res 2002;30:3141-3151.
#=GF RN [2]
#=GF RM 10529804
#=GF RT A conserved RNA structure element involved in the regulation of bacterial
#=GF RT riboflavin synthesis genes.
#=GF RA Gelfand MS, Mironov AA, Jomantas J, Kozlov YI, Perumov DA
#=GF RL Trends Genet 1999;15:439-442.
#=GF RN [3]
#=GF RM 12456892
#=GF RT An mRNA structure that controls gene expression by binding FMN.
#=GF RA Winkler WC, Cohen-Chalamish S, Breaker RR
#=GF RL Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A 2002;99:15908-15913.
#=GF RN [4]
#=GF RM 19169240
#=GF RT Coenzyme recognition and gene regulation by a flavin mononucleotide
#=GF RT riboswitch.
#=GF RA Serganov A, Huang L, Patel DJ
#=GF RL Nature. 2009;458:233-237.
#=GF RN [5]
#=GF RM 33103111
#=GF RT FMN riboswitch aptamer symmetry facilitates conformational switching
#=GF RT through mutually exclusive coaxial stacking configurations.
#=GF RA Wilt HM, Yu P, Tan K, Wang YX, Stagno JR
#=GF RL J Struct Biol X. 2020;4:100035.
#=GF CC The RFN element is a highly conserved domain that is found frequently in
#=GF CC the 5'-untranslated regions of prokaryotic mRNAs that encode for flavin
#=GF CC mononucleotide (FMN) biosynthesis and transport proteins. This element is
#=GF CC a metabolite-dependent riboswitch that directly binds FMN in the absence
#=GF CC of proteins. In Bacillus subtilis, the riboswitch most likely controls
#=GF CC gene expression by causing premature transcription termination within the
#=GF CC 5' untranslated region of the ribDEAHT operon and precluding access to the
#=GF CC ribosome-binding site of ypaA mRNA [3].The FMN riboswitch structure,
#=GF CC reported in [4] present an FMN-bound six-stem junction, adopts a
#=GF CC butterfly-like scaffold, stapled together by opposingly directed but
#=GF CC nearly identically folded peripheral domains. The FMN riboswitch structure
#=GF CC was reported in PDB: 3F2Q, 3F2T, 3F2W, 3F2X, 3F2Y, 3F30 [4] 6WJR, 6WJS [5]
#=GF WK FMN_riboswitch
#=GF SQ 146

